.env
state.json

# Your vault is your data, not the project's. Tracking it meant `git pull`
# could resurrect notes you deleted and `git stash` could undo your edits —
# both of which happened — and it put real business notes one `git commit`
# away from a public repository. `seed_vault.py` writes the sample on demand.
vault/*.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
raw-*.log

# skills installer writes a symlink farm per agent; keep .agents (real content)
# plus .claude (what Claude Code reads) and drop the rest
.hermes/
.kiro/
.bridge.pid
